Embedded React: a paint-free container that only moves damages nothing itself.

Modified from Embedded React (Apache-2.0, Copyright 2026 Cory Lamming) at the
revision pinned in dependencies.lock.json, after the patches listed before this
one there. Changed files: engine/scene/er_node_internal.h,
engine/scene/compositor.c, engine/tests/rendering/CMakeLists.txt and the new
engine/tests/rendering/test_paint_free_container.c. Proposed upstream as pull
request #315.

The damage pre-pass damaged the whole box of every node whose screen rect
changed. A list that grows at its unseen end (a VirtualList filling rows, a
taller spacer) changes its container's height every frame of a scroll, and the
container's box clipped to the viewport is the whole viewport: a full repaint
per frame where the scroll copy would repaint a strip. A container that paints
nothing (no background, border, opacity, gradient, shadow or complex
transform), painted nothing last time, does not clip its children and only
moved or resized now adds no damage of its own; its children report their own
moves. Each node records whether its last paint was such an empty one.

